<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ language }}" dir="{{ direction }}">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>{% block title %}{{ copy.product }}{% endblock %}</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/beta/assets/journey.css">
</head>
<body data-step="{{ step }}" data-language="{{ language }}">
  <a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">{{ copy.skip }}</a>
  {#
    The persistent frame, deliberately thinner than the shell's: a task mode has one exit, not a
    menu. The brand leaves for `/app` because `/beta/{language}` is the journey's own entry and
    `common.js` reconciles it straight back to whichever step the session is on -- a link that
    returned the reader to where they already were.

    **No organization identity here, and that is a boundary rather than an omission.**
    `open_commercial_session` takes an opaque `owner_id` and nothing else, so that "no `account_id`,
    `organization_id`, name, slug, or email reaches this function" and `FR-032`/`FR-033` hold *by
    absence rather than by inspection*. Routing a display name into this template would convert a
    guarantee held by absence into one held by inspection. The product decision to show it is made;
    the authority is not, and `RCA-002` disclaims the journey surface while no `RRA` specification
    governs its chrome. Reserve nothing and render nothing until that gap closes.
  #}
  <header class="site-header">
    <a class="brand" href="/app/{{ language }}" aria-label="{{ copy.frame_home_label }}">
      <span>KHEPRI</span>
    </a>
    {#
      Navigation, not a form: leaving deletes nothing, cancels nothing, and stops no job, so it
      carries no method and asks for no confirmation. The hint is what makes that legible instead of
      merely true -- a reader who thinks an exit discards their upload will not use it. The full
      label stays the accessible name at every width; only the visible text shortens.
    #}
    <a class="leave-analysis" href="/app/{{ language }}" aria-label="{{ copy.leave_analysis }}">
      <span class="leave-analysis-full">{{ copy.leave_analysis }}</span>
      <span class="leave-analysis-short" aria-hidden="true">{{ copy.leave_analysis_short }}</span>
    </a>
    <nav aria-label="{{ copy.language_navigation }}">
      <a class="language-link" href="/beta/{{ alternate }}/{{ step }}"
         lang="{{ alternate }}">{{ copy.language }}</a>
    </nav>
  </header>
  <nav class="step-nav" aria-label="{{ copy.journey_progress }}">
    <ol>
      <li class="{% if step == 'upload' %}current{% endif %}"><a href="/beta/{{ language }}/upload"><span>1</span> {{ copy.step_upload }}</a></li>
      <li class="{% if step == 'review' %}current{% endif %}"><a href="/beta/{{ language }}/review"><span>2</span> {{ copy.step_review }}</a></li>
      <li class="{% if step == 'processing' %}current{% endif %}"><a href="/beta/{{ language }}/processing"><span>3</span> {{ copy.step_processing }}</a></li>
      <li class="{% if step == 'report' %}current{% endif %}"><a href="/beta/{{ language }}/report"><span>4</span> {{ copy.step_report }}</a></li>
    </ol>
  </nav>
  <main id="main-content" class="journey-shell" tabindex="-1">
    {% block content %}{% endblock %}
  </main>
  <footer class="site-footer"><p>{{ copy.retention }}</p></footer>
  <script type="module" src="/beta/assets/common.js"></script>
  {% block script %}{% endblock %}
</body>
</html>
